{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-remote/src/remote.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T20:30:49.035499Z","id":"ec87dfce4ee275181da0d6386f4a55d8b431a8a6e591ab2970430106818f16c0","body":{"detail":"poll_previews acknowledges what the sink took. HostPreviews holds a preview only while a propose call is in this process (Deps::fix_coming). If a tick yields in a proposal whose job then finishes, and a poll reads the preview's event before the next tick records the fix, ServerHost::preview_ready finds no fix (set_fix_verify_url answers false), answers Ok, and the event is acknowledged, so the reporter never gets the link. The next tick is due at once and a preview takes a deploy's time, so the window is small.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":329},"end":{"line":372},"content_hash":"ba98c1b701a7bc35d2ca00468a257a39b307979a682c6a97efd09b65481fab69"},"suggested_fix":"Poll after the alarm's ticks, or have the sink answer an error when the run has a begun proposal and no fix, so the event stays with the service.","summary":"A preview told between a proposal's job ending and its fix being recorded is acknowledged and lost","tags":["review","session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-remote/src/remote.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T20:30:49.035550Z","id":"ee3707e71f52db777c91bf644ee1c4f6eb23929233b557473687719bff893d88","body":{"detail":"job and resume_exec poll with no pause of their own: GET /v1/jobs/{key}?wait=20 is expected to hold the request (crates/clax-bot-remote/src/wire.rs). A service that ignores wait burns the Durable Object's CPU, whose alarm limit is 30 seconds, until the tick yields. A service built on this wire must hold the poll.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":298},"end":{"line":322},"content_hash":"3d58a3c93e64dd057cebaaff67f59735b196275d31b5bd3e915417285bcab469"},"summary":"A service that answers a poll at once with running makes this loop spin","tags":["review","session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-remote/src/wire.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T20:30:49.035660Z","id":"6a86f707d6b045f56be12f87416e3184389486562547b861aad96181b9bb7b36","body":{"detail":"With a snapshot in hand, an unlisted run gets others, as ContainerWorkspace::offer answers for a queue with no target; only having no snapshot at all is unsure. Unsure for every unlisted queue would make each plain artifact run and each report on a queue with no target read as confidential on an instance with a service. The cost: a target added since the last snapshot reads as others until the next refresh.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":171},"end":{"line":185},"content_hash":"b5e06d14545f411d588d91ab1f42160bd2b9789b9a174da75cd8185990c9feb4"},"summary":"Offer::unsure for any queue or run a snapshot does not list, in place of Snapshot::others","tags":["revisit:when a service's targets change often enough that a stale others offer is seen","session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-remote/src/remote.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T21:07:58.241561Z","id":"22160a3a109ff6d83205c0fbd0cba08ddc8caba97a0ee7f6b37b6fca3a7098d3","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"The service holds the poll: Service::poll in crates/clax-bot-workspace-service/src/jobs.rs waits up to wait, at most MAX_WAIT_SECS. Evidence: bazelisk test //crates/clax-bot-workspace-service:integration, jobs::a_poll_is_held_for_its_wait_and_no_longer_than_the_most and jobs::a_host_waiting_on_a_long_command_asks_a_few_times_and_does_not_spin pass; the first fails with the wait replaced by Duration::ZERO.","supersedes":"ee3707e71f52db777c91bf644ee1c4f6eb23929233b557473687719bff893d88","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-remote/src/remote.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T21:41:04.598183Z","id":"df78a19c5043841eca11fc9770e265c67aa5173e7844b3b3c0b2bee83a71efeb","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"A word for a run with a begun, unanswered proposal is refused with CODE_FIX_COMING (HostPreviews::no_fix_yet, crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs) and poll_previews neither acknowledges nor counts it. Tests: resumable::a_preview_told_before_its_fix_is_refused_until_the_fix_is_there, remote::a_word_waiting_for_its_fix_stays_uncounted_and_unacknowledged.","supersedes":"ec87dfce4ee275181da0d6386f4a55d8b431a8a6e591ab2970430106818f16c0","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-remote/src/remote.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T21:41:04.905531Z","id":"19feb7643eb764bcff7bdd8750b71ef54593fd2790c40c41efc96c4b4f69a734","body":{"detail":"A run whose offer reads unsure gets a system prompt with no shell, written once at its first turn (Tick::turn in crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs). If the service returns while the run is working, offer() answers again but nothing tells the model, so it finishes without a shell it now has. Telling it takes a message in the run history at a turn boundary, across run.rs and prompt.rs.","kind":"concern","summary":"A run started during a service outage is not told when the shell comes back","tags":["review","session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-remote/src/remote.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T21:41:04.905568Z","id":"61aac5f45dfb769e72336bf54aaa7da3430016eb87b59d2bb9e1029c176c793d","body":{"detail":"A proposal counts as begun from its first request, so RemoteWorkspace::job waits out an outage rather than answering. A run that proposes during a long outage yields tick after tick until max_run_minutes, then stops with PROPOSAL_STRANDED even if nothing was pushed. The alternative, failing the first POST at once, risks a second branch when only the answer was lost.","kind":"concern","summary":"A proposal during an outage holds its run until the run cap","tags":["review","session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-remote/src/remote.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T23:16:35.120354Z","id":"0a8c227792b7f3ff9bd4b6aa33481636e0d730ef109c62593cf85cd7f0e4a8d1","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs reads Kept with serde_json::from_str(..).ok(), and Kept.snapshot holds offers in OfferForm, whose fields are all required and none unknown (crates/clax-bot-remote/src/wire.rs). A release that adds a field to Offer makes every stored Kept unreadable, and the Worker starts from None: the snapshot was to go anyway, but unfinished (ends the service never answered), preview_tries, poll_failed and tend_failures go with it. A lost unfinished entry leaves a run's container to the next reap; a lost preview_tries restarts the count. Reading the snapshot apart from the rest, so that only it fails closed, would keep them.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":140},"end":{"line":160},"content_hash":"213d228674ffbd70009d019f163c001a053efdd844227926a4722d64ed9b5b10"},"summary":"Kept is dropped whole when its snapshot stops parsing, so a change to Offer loses unfinished ends and tend backoff too","tags":["hosted","session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
